<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-BLOCK-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-BLOCK-002" ;
  triage:title "Local ingress does not validate/strip authenticated_source_host, allowing forged peer-authenticated status" ;
  triage:description "ApiRouter::route (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:919-939) only rejects AuthenticatedIngress::Local writes carrying origin_message_id/origin_timestamp; it never rejects or strips authenticated_source_host on Local ingress. WriteRequest.authenticated_source_host (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:70-74) is documented as 'not trusted from wire JSON' but commit 95dbb094 broadened its consumer from a host-equality check to a bare presence check: is_same_host_peer_receipt -> is_authenticated_peer_receipt (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:570-572) now returns true whenever authenticated_source_host.is_some(), with no host comparison. validate_non_self_recipient (crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs:930-952) takes an authenticated_peer_ingress bool and skips self-address rejection whenever true. PostWriteRouter::dispatch (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_delivery_router.rs:20-34) unconditionally takes the 'authenticated peer receipt' local-post-write branch whenever authenticated_source_host.is_some(), bypassing the normal host-based peer-delivery branch regardless of actual destination. Because Local ingress never validates/strips this field, any local caller (buggy client, stale/reused WriteRequest, or same-host adversary) can set authenticated_source_host on an ordinary local write to (1) bypass self-addressed-send rejection and (2) force the post-write router down the 'already a peer receipt' branch even for a legitimately host-qualified remote recipient, silently skipping actual outbound HTTPS peer delivery (message loss) while still reporting success. This is undocumented per RULE-012 (no ADR/boundary-record update accompanies this widened trust semantic)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture/security-boundary" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T20:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T20:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-BLOCK-002/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

